{
  "doc": "docs/behaviour/retailer.md",
  "issues": [
    {
      "does": "How the office takes on staff of its own: it puts the posts on the jobs board at the wage given, for people to apply, and the office then offers employment to those it takes on. It commits no money until someone is taken on.",
      "fields": {
        "account": {
          "description": "The account the wages are paid from, where the office itself pays them.",
          "type": "account"
        },
        "period": {
          "description": "The pay period: how often the wage is paid.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "duration"
        },
        "posts": {
          "description": "How many posts this advertisement is for.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "count"
        },
        "wage": {
          "description": "The wage for each pay period.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "amount"
        }
      },
      "form": "job_advertisement",
      "title": "Job advertisement",
      "writes": {
        "data": {
          "industry": "@industry",
          "openings": "=posts",
          "period": "=period",
          "role": "@role",
          "space": "@workplace",
          "wage": "#wage",
          "workplace": "@workplace_structure"
        },
        "kind": "job_posting",
        "offer": {
          "available": "=posts",
          "by": "=self",
          "take_up": "apply",
          "terms": {
            "commitments": [
              {
                "does": {
                  "outcome": {
                    "money": {
                      "amount": "=wage",
                      "for": "wages",
                      "from": "=account"
                    }
                  }
                },
                "every": "=period",
                "who": "=self"
              },
              "@occupancy"
            ],
            "template": "employment",
            "termination": "@termination"
          },
          "to": {
            "min_age_years": 18
          }
        },
        "text": "Hiring: {wage} every {period}."
      }
    },
    {
      "does": "How the office buys from a supplier, the outside world's market among them: it places the order at the seller's listed price. The form pays nothing by itself: pay the whole sum into the account the seller's price list names, at the same sitting. The seller delivers once an order is paid in full, sends back money that comes with no order waiting for it, and declines an order unpaid after a week.",
      "fields": {
        "account": {
          "description": "The account the order is paid from.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "account"
        },
        "at": {
          "description": "Where they are to be delivered.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "structure"
        },
        "deliver_to": {
          "description": "Who is to receive them.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "entity"
        },
        "for_days": {
          "description": "How many days the order may be served over.",
          "type": "count"
        },
        "kind": {
          "description": "What is ordered.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "text"
        },
        "quantity": {
          "description": "How many.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "count"
        },
        "retry_of": {
          "description": "An earlier order this one repeats.",
          "type": "record"
        },
        "seller": {
          "description": "Whom it is ordered from.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "entity"
        },
        "unit_price": {
          "description": "The price of each, as the seller advertises it.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "amount"
        }
      },
      "form": "order",
      "title": "An order to a supplier, paid with the order",
      "writes": {
        "data": {
          "account": "=account",
          "at": "=at",
          "deliver_to": "=deliver_to",
          "for_days": "=for_days",
          "kind": "=kind",
          "quantity": "=quantity",
          "retry_of": "=retry_of",
          "unit_price": "#unit_price"
        },
        "kind": "order",
        "text": "Order: {quantity} {kind} at {unit_price} each, delivered to {deliver_to} at {at}. Paid with this order.",
        "to": [
          "=seller"
        ],
        "visible": [
          "=self",
          "=seller"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "fields": {
        "buyer": {
          "description": "Who ordered.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "entity"
        },
        "declined": {
          "description": "Where nothing was delivered because the order was not paid for, or the buyer had not paid what it owed on earlier ones.",
          "options": [
            "unpaid",
            "overdue"
          ],
          "type": "choice"
        },
        "delivered": {
          "description": "How many were delivered.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "count"
        },
        "kind": {
          "description": "What was ordered.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "text"
        },
        "order": {
          "description": "The order.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "record"
        },
        "ordered": {
          "description": "How many were ordered.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "count"
        },
        "refund": {
          "description": "What was refunded for those not delivered.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "amount"
        }
      },
      "form": "delivery_note",
      "title": "A delivery note for an order served",
      "writes": {
        "basis": "=order",
        "data": {
          "declined": "=declined",
          "delivered": "=delivered",
          "kind": "=kind",
          "order": "=order",
          "ordered": "=ordered",
          "refund": "#refund"
        },
        "kind": "delivery_note",
        "text": "Delivered: {delivered} of {ordered} {kind} (order {order}).",
        "to": [
          "=buyer"
        ],
        "visible": [
          "=buyer",
          "=self"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "fields": {
        "claim": {
          "description": "The claim answered.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "record"
        },
        "rise_bps": {
          "description": "The rise offered, in hundredths of a percent.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "count"
        },
        "union": {
          "description": "The union that made the claim.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "entity"
        },
        "why": {
          "description": "Why that much.",
          "type": "text"
        }
      },
      "form": "wage_offer",
      "title": "An answer to a union's wage claim",
      "writes": {
        "basis": "=claim",
        "data": {
          "claim": "=claim",
          "employer": "=self",
          "rise_bps": "=rise_bps",
          "why": "=why"
        },
        "kind": "wage_offer",
        "text": "We offer a rise of {rise_bps} hundredths of a percent, in answer to {claim}.",
        "to": [
          "=union"
        ],
        "visible": [
          "=self",
          "=union"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "fields": {
        "account": {
          "description": "The account it is to be paid into.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "account"
        },
        "amount": {
          "description": "The sum invoiced.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "amount"
        },
        "buyer": {
          "description": "Who is invoiced.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "entity"
        },
        "from_at": {
          "description": "Where they were sent from.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "structure"
        },
        "kind": {
          "description": "What was sent.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "text"
        },
        "memo": {
          "description": "What the payment is for, in a few words.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "text"
        },
        "offer": {
          "description": "The buyer's standing offer it is sent under.",
          "type": "record"
        },
        "quantity": {
          "description": "How many.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "count"
        }
      },
      "form": "export_invoice",
      "title": "An invoice for goods sent to a buyer",
      "writes": {
        "basis": "=offer",
        "data": {
          "from_at": "=from_at",
          "kind": "=kind",
          "outcome": {
            "money": {
              "amount": "=amount",
              "for": "=memo",
              "to": "=account"
            }
          },
          "quantity": "=quantity"
        },
        "kind": "invoice",
        "text": "Invoice: {quantity} {kind}, {amount}.",
        "to": [
          "=buyer"
        ],
        "visible": [
          "=self",
          "=buyer"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "fields": {
        "account": {
          "description": "The account to be paid into if it is recovered.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "account"
        },
        "at": {
          "description": "Where from.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "structure"
        },
        "kind": {
          "description": "What was taken.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "text"
        },
        "quantity": {
          "description": "How many.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "count"
        },
        "value": {
          "description": "What it was worth.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "amount"
        }
      },
      "form": "crime_report",
      "title": "A report of goods taken, to the police",
      "writes": {
        "data": {
          "account": "=account",
          "at": "=at",
          "kind": "=kind",
          "quantity": "=quantity",
          "value": "#value"
        },
        "kind": "crime_report",
        "sends": [
          {
            "to": [
              "@police"
            ],
            "why": "The police investigate what is reported to them."
          }
        ],
        "text": "Report: {quantity} {kind} taken from {at}.",
        "to": [
          "@police"
        ],
        "visible": [
          "=self",
          "@police"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "does": "Answers someone who has asked the office in writing to put something right: yes or no, and where money is owed them and paid, how much. It does nothing by itself: what puts the thing right (a payment, a repair ordered, a paper withdrawn) is done besides.",
      "fields": {
        "amount": {
          "description": "Where money is owed them and paid: how much.",
          "type": "amount"
        },
        "asker": {
          "description": "Who asked.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "entity"
        },
        "granted": {
          "description": "Whether it will be put right.",
          "options": [
            "yes",
            "no"
          ],
          "required": true,
          "type": "choice"
        },
        "matter": {
          "description": "What it is about, in the word the request uses.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "text"
        },
        "reason": {
          "description": "Where it is refused: why.",
          "type": "text"
        },
        "request": {
          "description": "The request answered.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "record"
        }
      },
      "form": "remedy_answer",
      "title": "Answer to a request to put something right",
      "writes": {
        "basis": "=request",
        "data": {
          "amount": "#amount",
          "granted": "?granted",
          "matter": "=matter",
          "reason": "=reason",
          "request": "=request"
        },
        "kind": "remedy_answer",
        "text": "Answer to your request {request}: {granted}.",
        "to": [
          "=asker"
        ],
        "visible": [
          "=asker",
          "=self"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "does": "Answers a body that has told the office of an application against it, from the office's own books: what they show is owed, whether the thing is done, whether the paper complained of was wrong. The body decides on it when the time to answer has run; with no answer it decides in default.",
      "fields": {
        "applicant": {
          "description": "Who applied.",
          "type": "entity"
        },
        "application": {
          "description": "The application answered.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "record"
        },
        "done": {
          "description": "For a thing to be put right: whether it is done.",
          "options": [
            "yes",
            "no"
          ],
          "type": "choice"
        },
        "known": {
          "description": "Whether the office's books say anything of it.",
          "options": [
            "yes",
            "no"
          ],
          "required": true,
          "type": "choice"
        },
        "owed": {
          "description": "What the books show is owed the applicant (nought: nothing).",
          "type": "amount"
        },
        "statement": {
          "description": "What the office says in answer, in its own words, where these do not say it (what it disputes, and why).",
          "type": "text"
        },
        "venue": {
          "description": "The body that sent the notice.",
          "required": true,
          "type": "entity"
        },
        "wrong": {
          "description": "For a paper complained of: whether it was wrong.",
          "options": [
            "yes",
            "no"
          ],
          "type": "choice"
        }
      },
      "form": "complaint_answer",
      "title": "Answer to a desk's notice of an application against the office",
      "writes": {
        "basis": "=application",
        "data": {
          "application": "=application",
          "done": "?done",
          "known": "?known",
          "owed": "#owed",
          "statement": "=statement",
          "wrong": "?wrong"
        },
        "kind": "complaint_response",
        "text": "Answer on {application}.",
        "to": [
          "=venue"
        ],
        "visible": [
          "=venue",
          "=self",
          "=applicant"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "does": "Answers a body that has told the office of an application against it, from the office's own books: what they show is owed, whether the thing is done, whether the paper complained of was wrong. The body decides on it when the time to answer has run; with no answer it decides in default.",
      "fields": {
